 cmplx
      " (source) import-path: cmplx
      " (description) Package cmplx provides basic constants and mathematical functions for complex numbers. Special case handling conforms to the C99 standard Annex G IEC 60559-compatible complex arithmetic.
@sep1 Functions in cmplx
      Abs
           " (def) "func Abs(x complex128) float64"
           " (description) "Abs returns the absolute value (also called the modulus) of x."
      Acos
           " (def) "func Acos(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Acos returns the inverse cosine of x.
      Acosh
           " (def) "func Acosh(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Acosh returns the inverse hyperbolic cosine of x.
      Asin
           " (def) "func Asin(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Asin returns the inverse sine of x.
      Asinh
           " (def) "func Asinh(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Asinh returns the inverse hyperbolic sine of x.
      Atan
           " (def) "func Atan(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Atan returns the inverse tangent of x.
      Atanh
           " (def) "func Atanh(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Atanh returns the inverse hyperbolic tangent of x.
      Conj
           " (def) "func Conj(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Conj returns the complex conjugate of x.
      Cos
           " (def) "func Cos(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Cos returns the cosine of x.
      Cosh
           " (def) "func Cosh(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Cosh returns the hyperbolic cosine of x.
      Cot
           " (def) "func Cot(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Cot returns the cotangent of x.
      Exp
           " (def) "func Exp(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) "Exp returns e x, the base-e exponential of x."
      Inf
           " (def) "func Inf() complex128"
           " (description) "Inf returns a complex infinity, complex(+Inf, +Inf)."
      IsInf
           " (def) "func IsInf(x complex128) bool"
           " (description) "IsInf reports whether either real(x) or imag(x) is an infinity."
      IsNaN
           " (def) "func IsNaN(x complex128) bool"
           " (description) "IsNaN reports whether either real(x) or imag(x) is NaN and neither is an infinity."
      Log
           " (def) "func Log(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Log returns the natural logarithm of x.
      Log10
           " (def) "func Log10(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Log10 returns the decimal logarithm of x.
      NaN
           " (def) "func NaN() complex128"
           " (description) NaN returns a complex “not-a-number” value.
      Phase
           " (def) "func Phase(x complex128) float64"
           " (description) "Phase returns the phase (also called the argument) of x. The returned value is in the range [-Pi, Pi]."
      Polar
           " (def) "func Polar(x complex128) (r, θ float64)"
           " (description) "Polar returns the absolute value r and phase θ of x, such that x  equals  r * e θi. The phase is in the range [-Pi, Pi]."
      Pow
           " (def) "func Pow(x, y complex128) complex128"
           " (description) "Pow returns x y, the base-x exponential of y. For generalized compatibility with math.Pow:"
      Rect
           " (def) "func Rect(r, θ float64) complex128"
           " (description) Rect returns the complex number x with polar coordinates r, θ.
      Sin
           " (def) "func Sin(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Sin returns the sine of x.
      Sinh
           " (def) "func Sinh(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Sinh returns the hyperbolic sine of x.
      Sqrt
           " (def) "func Sqrt(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) "Sqrt returns the square root of x. The result r is chosen so that real(r) ≥ 0 and imag(r) has the same sign as imag(x)."
      Tan
           " (def) "func Tan(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Tan returns the tangent of x.
      Tanh
           " (def) "func Tanh(x complex128) complex128"
           " (description) Tanh returns the hyperbolic tangent of x.

 rand
      " (source) import-path: rand
      " (description) Package rand implements pseudo-random number generators suitable for tasks such as simulation, but it should not be used for security-sensitive work.
@sep1 Functions in rand
      ExpFloat64
           " (def) "func ExpFloat64() float64"
      Float32
           " (def) "func Float32() float32"
           " (description) "Float32 returns, as a float32, a pseudo-random number in the half-open interval [0.0,1.0) from the default Source."
      Float64
           " (def) "func Float64() float64"
           " (description) "Float64 returns, as a float64, a pseudo-random number in the half-open interval [0.0,1.0) from the default Source."
      Int
           " (def) "func Int() int"
           " (description) Int returns a non-negative pseudo-random int from the default Source.
      Int31
           " (def) "func Int31() int32"
           " (description) Int31 returns a non-negative pseudo-random 31-bit integer as an int32 from the default Source.
      Int31n
           " (def) "func Int31n(n int32) int32"
           " (description) "Int31n returns, as an int32, a non-negative pseudo-random number in the half-open interval [0,n) from the default Source. It panics if n  LTE  0."
      Int63
           " (def) "func Int63() int64"
           " (description) Int63 returns a non-negative pseudo-random 63-bit integer as an int64 from the default Source.
      Int63n
           " (def) "func Int63n(n int64) int64"
           " (description) "Int63n returns, as an int64, a non-negative pseudo-random number in the half-open interval [0,n) from the default Source. It panics if n  LTE  0."
      Intn
           " (def) "func Intn(n int) int"
           " (description) "Intn returns, as an int, a non-negative pseudo-random number in the half-open interval [0,n) from the default Source. It panics if n  LTE  0."
      NormFloat64
           " (def) "func NormFloat64() float64"
      Perm
           " (def) "func Perm(n int) []int"
           " (description) "Perm returns, as a slice of n ints, a pseudo-random permutation of the integers in the half-open interval [0,n) from the default Source."
      Read
           " (def) "func Read(p []byte) (n int, err error)"
      Seed
           " (def) "func Seed(seed int64)"
      Shuffle
           " (def) "func Shuffle(n int, swap func(i, j int))"
      Uint32
           " (def) "func Uint32() uint32"
           " (description) Uint32 returns a pseudo-random 32-bit value as a uint32 from the default Source.
      Uint64
           " (def) "func Uint64() uint64"
           " (description) Uint64 returns a pseudo-random 64-bit value as a uint64 from the default Source.
@sep2 Types in rand
      Rand
           " (description) struct
           " (description) A Rand is a source of random numbers.
      Source
           " (description) interface
           " (description) "A Source represents a source of uniformly-distributed pseudo-random int64 values in the range [0, 1 LT  LT 63)."
