      " (description) Package debug contains facilities for programs to debug themselves while they are running.
@sep1 Functions in debug
      FreeOSMemory
           " (def) "func FreeOSMemory()"
      PrintStack
           " (def) "func PrintStack()"
           " (description) PrintStack prints to standard error the stack trace returned by runtime.Stack.
      ReadGCStats
           " (def) "func ReadGCStats(stats *GCStats)"
      SetCrashOutput
           " (def) "func SetCrashOutput(f *os.File, opts CrashOptions) error"
      SetGCPercent
           " (def) "func SetGCPercent(percent int) int"
      SetMaxStack
           " (def) "func SetMaxStack(bytes int) int"
      SetMaxThreads
           " (def) "func SetMaxThreads(threads int) int"
      SetMemoryLimit
           " (def) "func SetMemoryLimit(limit int64) int64"
           " (description) SetMemoryLimit provides the runtime with a soft memory limit.
      SetPanicOnFault
           " (def) "func SetPanicOnFault(enabled bool) bool"
      SetTraceback
           " (def) "func SetTraceback(level string)"
      Stack
           " (def) "func Stack() []byte"
           " (description) Stack returns a formatted stack trace of the goroutine that calls it. It calls runtime.Stack with a large enough buffer to capture the entire trace.
      WriteHeapDump
           " (def) "func WriteHeapDump(fd uintptr)"
           " (description) WriteHeapDump writes a description of the heap and the objects in it to the given file descriptor.
@sep2 Types in debug
      BuildInfo
           " (description) struct
           " (description) BuildInfo represents the build information read from a Go binary.
      BuildSetting
           " (description) struct
           " (description) A BuildSetting is a key-value pair describing one setting that influenced a build.
      CrashOptions
           " (description) struct
           " (description) CrashOptions provides options that control the formatting of the fatal crash message.
      GCStats
           " (description) struct
           " (description) GCStats collect information about recent garbage collections.
      Module
           " (description) struct
           " (description) A Module describes a single module included in a build.

 metrics
      " (source) import-path: metrics
      " (description) Package metrics provides a stable interface to access implementation-defined metrics exported by the Go runtime. This package is similar to existing functions like runtime.ReadMemStats and runtime/debug.ReadGCStats, but significantly more general.
@sep1 Functions in metrics
      Read
           " (def) "func Read(m []Sample)"
           " (description) Read populates each Value field in the given slice of metric samples.
@sep2 Types in metrics
      Description
           " (description) struct
           " (description) Description describes a runtime metric.
      Float64Histogram
           " (description) struct
           " (description) Float64Histogram represents a distribution of float64 values.
      Sample
           " (description) struct
           " (description) Sample captures a single metric sample.
      Value
           " (description) struct
           " (description) Value represents a metric value returned by the runtime.
      ValueKind
           " (description) other
           " (description) ValueKind is a tag for a metric Value which indicates its type.

 pprof
      " (source) import-path: pprof
      " (description) Package pprof writes runtime profiling data in the format expected by the pprof visualization tool.
@sep1 Functions in pprof
      Do
           " (def) "func Do(ctx context.Context, labels LabelSet, f func(context.Context))"
      ForLabels
           " (def) "func ForLabels(ctx context.Context, f func(key, value string) bool)"
           " (description) ForLabels invokes f with each label set on the context. The function f should return true to continue iteration or false to stop iteration early.
      Label
           " (def) "func Label(ctx context.Context, key string) (string, bool)"
           " (description) Label returns the value of the label with the given key on ctx, and a boolean indicating whether that label exists.
      SetGoroutineLabels
           " (def) "func SetGoroutineLabels(ctx context.Context)"
      StartCPUProfile
           " (def) "func StartCPUProfile(w io.Writer) error"
      StopCPUProfile
           " (def) "func StopCPUProfile()"
           " (description) StopCPUProfile stops the current CPU profile, if any. StopCPUProfile only returns after all the writes for the profile have completed.
      WithLabels
           " (def) "func WithLabels(ctx context.Context, labels LabelSet) context.Context"
           " (description) WithLabels returns a new context.Context with the given labels added. A label overwrites a prior label with the same key.
      WriteHeapProfile
           " (def) "func WriteHeapProfile(w io.Writer) error"
           " (description) "WriteHeapProfile is shorthand for Lookup('heap').WriteTo(w, 0). It is preserved for backwards compatibility."
@sep2 Types in pprof
      LabelSet
           " (description) struct
           " (description) LabelSet is a set of labels.
      Profile
           " (description) struct

