 sort
      " (source) import-path: sort
      " (description) Package sort provides primitives for sorting slices and user-defined collections.
@sep1 Functions in sort
      Find
           " (def) "func Find(n int, cmp func(int) int) (i int, found bool)"
      Float64s
           " (def) "func Float64s(x []float64)"
           " (description) "Float64s sorts a slice of float64s in increasing order. Not-a-number (NaN) values are ordered before other values."
      Float64sAreSorted
           " (def) "func Float64sAreSorted(x []float64) bool"
           " (description) "Float64sAreSorted reports whether the slice x is sorted in increasing order, with not-a-number (NaN) values before any other values."
      Ints
           " (def) "func Ints(x []int)"
           " (description) Ints sorts a slice of ints in increasing order.
      IntsAreSorted
           " (def) "func IntsAreSorted(x []int) bool"
           " (description) IntsAreSorted reports whether the slice x is sorted in increasing order.
      IsSorted
           " (def) "func IsSorted(data Interface) bool"
           " (description) IsSorted reports whether data is sorted.
      Search
           " (def) "func Search(n int, f func(int) bool) int"
      SearchFloat64s
           " (def) "func SearchFloat64s(a []float64, x float64) int"
      SearchInts
           " (def) "func SearchInts(a []int, x int) int"
      SearchStrings
           " (def) "func SearchStrings(a []string, x string) int"
      Slice
           " (def) "func Slice(x any, less func(i, j int) bool)"
           " (description) Slice sorts the slice x given the provided less function. It panics if x is not a slice.
      SliceIsSorted
           " (def) "func SliceIsSorted(x any, less func(i, j int) bool) bool"
           " (description) SliceIsSorted reports whether the slice x is sorted according to the provided less function. It panics if x is not a slice.
      SliceStable
           " (def) "func SliceStable(x any, less func(i, j int) bool)"
           " (description) SliceStable sorts the slice x using the provided less function, keeping equal elements in their original order. It panics if x is not a slice.
      Sort
           " (def) "func Sort(data Interface)"
      Stable
           " (def) "func Stable(data Interface)"
           " (description) Stable sorts data in ascending order as determined by the Less method, while keeping the original order of equal elements.
      Strings
           " (def) "func Strings(x []string)"
           " (description) Strings sorts a slice of strings in increasing order.
      StringsAreSorted
           " (def) "func StringsAreSorted(x []string) bool"
           " (description) StringsAreSorted reports whether the slice x is sorted in increasing order.
@sep2 Types in sort
      Float64Slice
           " (description) other
           " (description) "Float64Slice implements Interface for a []float64, sorting in increasing order, with not-a-number (NaN) values ordered before other values."
      IntSlice
           " (description) other
           " (description) IntSlice attaches the methods of Interface to []int, sorting in increasing order.
      Interface
           " (description) interface
      StringSlice
           " (description) other
           " (description) StringSlice attaches the methods of Interface to []string, sorting in increasing order.

