 time
      " (source) import-path: time
      " (description) Package time provides functionality for measuring and displaying time.
@sep1 Functions in time
      After
           " (def) "func After(d Duration)  LT -chan Time"
           " (description) "After waits for the duration to elapse and then sends the current time on the returned channel. It is equivalent to NewTimer(d).C."
      Sleep
           " (def) "func Sleep(d Duration)"
           " (description) Sleep pauses the current goroutine for at least the duration d. A negative or zero duration causes Sleep to return immediately.
      Tick
           " (def) "func Tick(d Duration)  LT -chan Time"
           " (description) "Tick is a convenience wrapper for NewTicker providing access to the ticking channel only. Unlike NewTicker, Tick will return nil if d  LTE  0."
